{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"coverage\":[{\"reason\":\"Sets operative SFC circular scope, instruments, exemption period and start date.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\"},{\"reason\":\"Explains original effective date, regulatory-arbitrage rationale and alignment context.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u1.381\"},{\"reason\":\"Describes EU background exemption and reporting conditions; not the SFC operative rule.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u3.801\"},{\"reason\":\"Describes UK background exemption and its indefinite duration; not the SFC operative rule.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u4.1019\"},{\"reason\":\"States that the Hong Kong Code provision will be amended and gazetted later, creating timing uncertainty.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357\"},{\"reason\":\"Contact instruction; no substantive applicability rule.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u7.1479\"},{\"reason\":\"Identifies issuing division; no substantive applicability rule.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u10.1587\"},{\"reason\":\"Identifies issuing authority; no substantive applicability rule.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u12.1614\"},{\"reason\":\"Document terminator; no substantive applicability rule.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u13.1649\"},{\"reason\":\"Circular identifier; no substantive applicability rule.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u14.1654\"},{\"reason\":\"Defines the referenced SFC margin requirements as Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671\"},{\"reason\":\"EU legal citation; supports explanatory background only.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u17.1837\"},{\"reason\":\"UK policy-statement citation; supports explanatory background only.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u19.1919\"},{\"reason\":\"Explains what BTS 2016/2251 refers to; supports UK background only.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u21.2176\"}],\"dimensions\":[{\"dimension\":\"scope\",\"explanation\":\"The operative text addresses licensed corporations and the listed non-centrally cleared equity options. It does not expressly state whether every licensed corporation counterparty, transaction capacity, or geographic booking location is included.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\",\"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671\"],\"status\":\"AMBIGUOUS\"},{\"dimension\":\"definitions\",\"explanation\":\"The circular defines the collective term “non-centrally cleared equity options” by listing single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options. It does not define “licensed corporation” beyond the Code reference.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\",\"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"exceptions\",\"explanation\":\"The exemption is stated for the listed instruments, but no additional conditions (such as reporting, monitoring, counterparty class or trade purpose) are stated in the SFC operative text. EU monitoring/reporting is described as foreign background and could be mistakenly treated as an SFC condition.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\",\"d802c45a4262c.u3.801\"],\"status\":\"AMBIGUOUS\"},{\"dimension\":\"modality\",\"explanation\":\"“Will exempt” announces an SFC decision, while the Code paragraph “will be amended accordingly and gazetted in due course” leaves the legal mechanism and interim force unresolved.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\",\"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357\"],\"status\":\"AMBIGUOUS\"},{\"dimension\":\"time\",\"explanation\":\"The announced period begins 4 January 2026 and lasts “until further notice”; the amendment is to be gazetted later, so the relationship between announcement date, commencement date and gazettal is unresolved.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\",\"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357\"],\"status\":\"AMBIGUOUS\"},{\"dimension\":\"dependencies\",\"explanation\":\"Applicability depends on instrument classification, absence of central clearing, licensed-corporation status, the Part III Schedule 10 requirement, and whether the circular operates before gazettal. EU and UK materials explain alignment but do not themselves determine SFC scope.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\",\"d802c45a4262c.u1.381\",\"d802c45a4262c.u3.801\",\"d802c45a4262c.u4.1019\",\"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357\",\"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671\"] ,\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"}],\"questions\":[\"Does the announced exemption have operative effect from 4 January 2026 before the Part III Schedule 10 amendment is gazetted?\",\"Does “licensed corporations” cover all transactions of a licensed corporation, including offshore booking or counterparties outside the SFC perimeter?\",\"Are any EU-style monitoring or reporting conditions intended to apply in Hong Kong, or are they explanatory background only?\",\"What precise contractual or product features determine that an option is a single-stock, equity-basket or equity-index option and is non-centrally cleared?\"] ,\"readings\":[{\"assumptions\":[\"The selected control concerns whether an SFC licensed corporation may treat a specified option exposure as exempt from the SFC margin requirement on a stated date.\",\"The option is classified as one of the three listed types and is not centrally cleared.\",\"No EU or UK condition is imported unless the SFC text expressly adopts it.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) issues this circular to inform licensed corporations that it will exempt non-centrally cleared single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options (collectively, “non-centrally cleared equity options”) from its margin requirements1 from 4 January 2026 until further notice to align with the latest global developments.\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\"},{\"quote\":\"As set out in Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671\"}],\"distinction\":\"Reading A treats the circular as an operative announcement: from 2026-01-04, the listed non-centrally cleared equity options are exempt for licensed corporations, despite the later gazettal statement. The foreign EU and UK provisions are alignment context only.\",\"family\":\"modality\",\"formalization\":{\"facts\":[{\"meaning\":\"The actor is a corporation licensed by or registered with the SFC under the Code of Conduct context.\",\"name\":\"licensed_corporation\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\",\"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"boolean\"},{\"meaning\":\"The transaction is a non-centrally cleared single-stock, equity-basket or equity-index option.\",\"name\":\"qualifying_non_cleared_equity_option\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"boolean\"},{\"meaning\":\"The assessment date is on or after 2026-01-04.\",\"name\":\"assessment_on_or_after_2026_01_04\",\"requires_judgment\":false,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"boolean\"},{\"meaning\":\"The announced exemption remains in force because no further notice ending it has been identified.\",\"name\":\"exemption_until_further_notice\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"boolean\"}],\"result\":\"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] The selected exemption condition is satisfied when the actor is a licensed corporation, the option qualifies, the assessment date is on or after 2026-01-04, and the exemption remains in force. False means at least one of those conditions is not established; it does not determine whether the underlying Code amendment has been gazetted.\",\"result_type\":\"bool\",\"scope\":\"A selected SFC margin-exemption control for one licensed corporation and one option exposure.\"},\"local_id\":\"reading_a\",\"questions\":[\"Whether the circular alone is legally sufficient before gazettal remains unresolved.\"],\"statement\":\"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Under the announced-operational reading, the selected SFC exemption condition is satisfied for a licensed corporation's qualifying non-centrally cleared equity option assessed on or after 2026-01-04 while the exemption remains in force.\" ,\"subject\":\"SFC margin-exemption applicability\"},{\"assumptions\":[\"The Code amendment and gazettal are prerequisites for operative legal exemption.\",\"The announcement signals intended future alignment but does not itself disapply the existing Part III requirement before gazettal.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"Paragraph 7(e) of Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct will be amended accordingly and gazetted in due course.\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357\"},{\"quote\":\"The margin requirements for non-centrally cleared equity options were originally scheduled to take effect on that date.\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u1.381\"},{\"quote\":\"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) issues this circular to inform licensed corporations that it will exempt non-centrally cleared single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options (collectively, “non-centrally cleared equity options”) from its margin requirements1 from 4 January 2026 until further notice to align with the latest global developments.\",\"unit_id\":\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\"}],\"distinction\":\"Reading B treats the circular as a prospective policy announcement whose operative effect depends on the promised Code amendment and gazettal. Before that event, the existing margin requirement remains applicable; after gazettal, the listed options are exempt from 2026-01-04 or the gazettal commencement date, whichever the amendment specifies.\",\"family\":\"time\",\"formalization\":null,\"local_id\":\"reading_b\",\"questions\":[\"The text does not state whether gazettal is constitutive, merely formal, or retroactive to 2026-01-04.\",\"The text does not specify the commencement date in the eventual amendment.\"],\"statement\":\"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Under the gazettal-dependent reading, the exemption condition is satisfied only once the required Code amendment has been gazetted and its commencement requirements are met; the circular alone does not establish that condition before then.\",\"subject\":\"SFC margin-exemption applicability\"}]}"}}
